    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38741" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prō-lŭbĭum</span></b> ,
			ĭi, n.
		lubet. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Subject.,
			<i>will</i>, <i>desire</i>, <i>inclination</i> (ante- and post-class.): muliebre
			ingenium, prolubium, occasio, Att. ap. <i><span class="en">Non.
				64, 8</span></i>; Novat. and <i><span class="en">Laber. ib.
			10</span></i> and 12; <i><span class="en">Ter. Ad. 5, 9, 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 16,
				19, 12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Object., <i>pleasure</i> (postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">majus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 5, 10, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libidinis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 249, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
